Ley line - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ley_line\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ley_line </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In Creation, there are flows of mystic energy. Like blood in a person's arteries or water in a river. You needn't &quot;do&quot; anything with them (but in Dynasty of Dovak, I used disruption of the local Dragon-lines to denote that a powerful sorcerous working had warped the very nature of reality to prompt the PCs to go investigate).<br /> <br /> Demesnes form on confluences of Dragon-lines, so if you want to build a manse you could do some geomancy to plot the best place to look.<br /> <br /> 2E had Charms that treated Dragon-lines like fibre-optic broadband. I don't recommend it.<br /> <br /> For most characters, it's just background estoria like ley lines in real life. It's something for crack-pots and mystics to rant about and academics to investigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T04:48:08-08:00","id":1369812,"title":"","content":"I've got a Shogunate era Earth Aspect whose trying to use ambient energy from them as the basis of a mass transit system on the basis that airship construction and maintinance is unsustainable long-term. The kind of land and resources necessary for such a thing requires a lot of negotiation and would probably be next to impossible to get off the ground in the Age of Sorrows unless you were the Scarlet Empress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T15:30:37-08:00","id":1369917,"title":"","content":"They are also the source of Exalted's version of Weapons of Mass Destruction. First Age scholars realized that you could build artifacts and perform sorceries to physically move leylines, stop them, or reverse them. This was a very bad idea. It tends to cause the kind of problems that require cartographers to redo a lot of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T15:52:10-08:00","id":1369919,"title":"","content":"The Second Edition book Oadenol\u2019s Codex has a chapter on Demesnes, Manses, 